      "title": "Addressing Capacity and Throttling Issues in Payment Gateway v2",
      "content_summary": "Guidance on diagnosing and resolving scaling failures, rate limit errors, and resource exhaustion within the Payment Gateway v2 and Billing Disputes Handler infrastructure.",
      "content_body": "When users report slow responses or rate limit exceeded errors, first verify the autoscaling group status for Payment Gateway v2. A common cause is a misconfigured rate limit policy that triggers prematurely under peak load, leading to throttling and perceived capacity limits. Investigate CPU usage spikes and memory leaks to determine if resource exhaustion is occurring due to insufficient capacity planning. To resolve, apply a configuration change to adjust the rate limits and initiate a capacity increase for the affected instances. Ensure that the Billing Disputes Handler is also monitored, as it shares underlying scaling resources."
